  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S. Usha Tea Co. & Anr vs The Corporation Of Calcutta & Ors on 16 June, 2021 Author: Tirthankar Ghosh Bench: Tirthankar Ghosh 16.06.2021 In The High Court At Calcutta Item No.11 Criminal Revisional Jurisdiction Ct.No.34 dc. C.R.R. 1112 of 1994 (Via Video Conference) M/s. Usha Tea Co. & Anr. versus The Corporation of Calcutta & Ors. In Re: An Application filed under Sections 401 and 482 read with Section 397 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973. Mr. Arindam Jana ... Mr. Anindya Sundar Chatterjee, Mr. Goutam Dinda ... For the K.M.C. Md. Anwar Hossain, Ms. Sreyashee Biswas ... For the State.",
    "facts": "The petitioners challenged this judgment and order passed in the said case before the learned Sessions Judge, VIIIth Bench, City Sessions Court, Calcutta in Criminal Appeal No. 23 of 1991. The revisional application has been pending since then. Having regard to the time so consumed by the court in considering and disposing of the revisional application, I am of the view that the petitioner no.2 has suffered from mental agony because of the sentence so imposed by the learned Senior Municipal Magistrate, Calcutta for almost 39 years.",
